# PocketJS on ArtInChip D13x / Luban-Lite.
#
# Gate 0 scope: this package currently ships the C/Rust ABI conformance probe
# only. The UI Core, the QuickJS engine and the renderer land here in later
# gates, once the RV32IMAFDC/ILP32D ABI is proven on real D133ECS silicon.

menuconfig LPKG_USING_POCKETJS
    bool "PocketJS (JavaScript runtime for ArtInChip D13x)"
    default n
    help
      Builds the PocketJS runtime for the ArtInChip D13x (Xuantie E907FDP,
      RV32IMAFDC / ILP32D hard-float).

      The Rust half is delivered as a prebuilt staticlib,
      libpocketjs_abi_probe.a, which is deliberately NOT committed. Produce it
      from the PocketJS repository before building:

        python hosts/rt-thread/ports/artinchip-d13x/tools/build-firmware.py

      If the archive is absent the SConscript fails with instructions rather
      than silently linking a firmware without a runtime.

if LPKG_USING_POCKETJS

config LPKG_POCKETJS_ABI_PROBE
    bool "Expose the pjs_abi / pjs_abi_panic MSH commands"
    default y
    help
      Registers the Gate 0 conformance probe at the MSH prompt. Turning this
      off builds the runtime without the probe, which is what a shipping
      configuration eventually wants.

config LPKG_POCKETJS_AUTORUN
    bool "Run the ABI probe once at boot"
    default y
    help
      Makes the Gate 0 evidence appear on the console without an operator at
      the prompt. Useful on bring-up hardware with no interactive terminal.

endif
